      "title": "Qwen Image 2.1 INT8 (convrot) + prompt enhancer — notes",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Qwen Image 2.1 INT8 (convrot) + prompt enhancer\n\nSame image pipeline as `qwen-image-2.1-int8.json`: UNET `qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot`, regular text encoder `qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot` on **CPU**, VAE BF16, 1024x1024, seed 42 fixed, 25 steps, cfg 1, euler/simple, prefix `Qwen_image_2.1_int8_enhanced`.\n\n**How to use.** Type a short prompt (any language) into *T2I Prompt Rewrite*. Its `positive_prompt` output feeds the `prompt` input of the regular encoder, so the image is generated from the expanded description. The two *Preview as Text* nodes show the rewritten prompt and `parse_ok`: `True` means the enhancer returned valid JSON and the shown text is the extracted `rewritten_prompt`; `False` means the raw model answer was passed through unparsed - re-run with another seed or shorten the prompt. Sampling defaults are upstream's (temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20, presence_penalty 1.5, max_new_tokens 16256, seed 42 fixed); changing any of them re-runs the enhancer. To bypass the enhancer, disconnect `positive_prompt -> prompt` and type into the encoder directly, as in the plain INT8 workflow.\n\n**Cost.** The brown CLIPLoader loads a *second*, separate model: the Comfy-Org prompt-enhancer checkpoint `qwen3.5_9b_qwen_image_2.1_pe_t2i.int8_convrot.safetensors` (Qwen3.5 9B, INT8, ~9.5 GB extra download) with type `qwen_image`, device `default`. `default` lets ComfyUI's model manager place it on the GPU and offload to the CPU as needed alongside the INT8 transformer within the 16 GiB RX 6950 XT and its 5 GiB reserve. Prompt rewriting is autoregressive generation of up to 16256 tokens, so it takes considerably longer than the image itself. The PE loader is *not* the encoder: do not swap the two CLIPLoaders, and leave the regular encoder on `cpu`."
      ]
    },
